cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The accretion pilot: memory, growth, and latent relevance in small evolving graphs"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained, bounded computational exploration of whether local structural change
  in small graphs can carry the memory of an imposed history while also opening new
  possibilities, whether such memory is locally accessible, and whether a later local
  change can make a dormant trace causally relevant again. Speculative exploratory
  register; every result is gated, with limitations and dated corrections kept in place.
  Two threads: (A) a use-reinforced, growth-capable substrate with a walker (v1-v14);
  (B) a walker-free self-rewriting graph grammar (endogenous growth).
type: dataset            # a mixed code + data + write-up snapshot; adjust to "software" if preferred
version: "2026.09.08"    # date-based snapshot version; bump on each deposit
date-released: "2026-09-08"
